# 🔥 Top 50 Vulnerability Patterns

## Category 1: Reentrancy (5 patterns)

### 1. Classic Reentrancy
```solidity
// VULNERABLE
function withdraw() external {
    uint256 balance = balances[msg.sender];
    (bool success,) = msg.sender.call{value: balance}("");  // External call BEFORE state update
    require(success);
    balances[msg.sender] = 0;  // State updated AFTER call
}

// SECURE: Checks-Effects-Interactions
function withdraw() external {
    uint256 balance = balances[msg.sender];
    balances[msg.sender] = 0;  // State updated BEFORE call
    (bool success,) = msg.sender.call{value: balance}("");
    require(success);
}
```

### 2. Cross-Function Reentrancy
Attack reenters via different function that reads stale state.

### 3. Cross-Contract Reentrancy  
Attack reenters via external contract that calls back.

### 4. Read-Only Reentrancy
Exploit stale view function data during callback (common in Curve/Balancer).

### 5. ERC777 Hooks Reentrancy
`tokensReceived` hook enables reentrancy on token transfers.

