## Category 2: Access Control (5 patterns)

### 6. Missing Access Control
```solidity
// VULNERABLE
function setAdmin(address _admin) external {
    admin = _admin;  // Anyone can call!
}

// SECURE
function setAdmin(address _admin) external onlyOwner {
    admin = _admin;
}
```

### 7. Incorrect Modifier Logic
```solidity
// VULNERABLE - missing return
modifier onlyOwner() {
    if (msg.sender != owner) { revert(); }
    _;  // Missing in some paths
}
```

### 8. tx.origin Authentication
```solidity
// VULNERABLE - phishing attack possible
require(tx.origin == owner);

// SECURE
require(msg.sender == owner);
```

### 9. Privilege Escalation
Users gaining higher permissions than intended.

### 10. Default Visibility (pre-0.8)
Functions defaulting to `public` instead of `internal`.

---

## Category 3: Integer Issues (5 patterns)

### 11. Integer Overflow (pre-0.8)
```solidity
// VULNERABLE (Solidity < 0.8)
uint8 x = 255;
x += 1;  // x = 0 (overflow)

// SECURE: Use SafeMath or Solidity >= 0.8
```

### 12. Precision Loss
```solidity
// VULNERABLE - division before multiplication
uint256 result = (a / b) * c;  // Loses precision

// SECURE
uint256 result = (a * c) / b;
```

### 13. Rounding Direction Exploitation
```solidity
// Favor protocol in divisions
uint256 shares = (amount * totalShares) / totalAssets;  // Rounds down
// Add 1 when rounding in user's favor would hurt protocol
```

### 14. Unsafe Casting
```solidity
// VULNERABLE
int8 signed = -1;
uint8 unsigned = uint8(signed);  // 255, not error!
```

### 15. Division by Zero
Missing checks before division operations.

