## Category 6: Logic Errors (5 patterns)

### 26. Wrong Comparison Operator
```solidity
// VULNERABLE
require(balance > 0);  // Should be >=

// Or off-by-one errors
for (uint i = 0; i <= length; i++)  // Should be <
```

### 27. Incorrect State Updates
Updating wrong variable or missing updates entirely.

### 28. Missing Return Value Check
```solidity
// VULNERABLE
token.transfer(to, amount);  // Some tokens return false

// SECURE
require(token.transfer(to, amount), "Transfer failed");
// Or use SafeERC20
```

### 29. Initialization Issues
```solidity
// VULNERABLE - can be called twice
function initialize() external {
    owner = msg.sender;
}

// SECURE
bool initialized;
function initialize() external {
    require(!initialized);
    initialized = true;
    owner = msg.sender;
}
```

### 30. Front-Running
Transactions can be reordered by miners for profit.

---

## Category 7: Token Issues (5 patterns)

### 31. Fee-on-Transfer Tokens
```solidity
// VULNERABLE - assumes amount received
token.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
balances[msg.sender] += amount;  // Wrong if token has fee

// SECURE
uint256 before = token.balanceOf(address(this));
token.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
uint256 received = token.balanceOf(address(this)) - before;
balances[msg.sender] += received;
```

### 32. Rebasing Tokens
Tokens that change balance automatically (stETH).

### 33. ERC20 Approval Race
Double-spend on `approve()` change.

### 34. Missing Return Value
Non-standard ERC20 tokens (USDT) don't return bool.

### 35. Blacklist Tokens
USDC/USDT can blacklist addresses.

---

## Category 8: DeFi-Specific (5 patterns)

### 36. First Depositor Attack
```solidity
// VULNERABLE vault
shares = (amount * totalShares) / totalAssets;
// Attacker: deposit 1 wei, donate, inflate share price

// SECURE: Virtual shares/assets
shares = (amount * (totalShares + 1e18)) / (totalAssets + 1e18);
```

### 37. Sandwich Attacks
Front-run user's swap → execute user's swap → back-run.

### 38. Liquidation Issues
Incorrect liquidation thresholds or incentives.

### 39. Slippage Exploitation
Missing or incorrect slippage protection.

### 40. MEV Extraction
Miners/bots extracting value from pending txs.

---

## Category 9: Proxy & Upgrade (5 patterns)

### 41. Storage Collision
```solidity
// Proxy and implementation use different storage slots
// Can overwrite critical data
```

### 42. Uninitialized Proxy
Implementation not initialized, can be taken over.

### 43. Function Selector Clash
Proxy and implementation have same selector.

### 44. Selfdestruct in Implementation
Can brick the proxy.

### 45. Upgrade Without Timelock
Instant malicious upgrades possible.

